    "result_text": "All 65 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. **Sequence counter** \u2014 added a static `AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`, incremented once per successful create, giving a monotonically increasing, gap-free `seq` shared across all creates on the singleton controller.\n\n2. **Event emission** \u2014 after the existing human-readable audit line, a second `AUDIT.info` line emits the JSON object:\n   ```json\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n\n3. **Immutable record `OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 a private Java `record` (immutable by construction) that serializes itself to a single JSON object, with proper JSON string escaping for the identifier value.\n\n4. **`primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper** \u2014 returns the owner's current primary identifier (today `customerCode`). This is the single seam the spec calls out: when the customer code is later unified into a member id, only this one method changes and the event automatically carries the `memberId` instead \u2014 the event value is sourced from here rather than hard-coded.\n\nThe new `Cp53Tests` passes (one AUDIT line contains the `OWNER_CREATED` marker, the owner id, and the current `customerCode`), and the full suite remains green at 65/65.",
